From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:23:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06924/11362] [outer-loop] sk48: L5 SOLVED round 9 (codex,
 first attempt at fresh territory)

Round-9 gpt-5.6-sol session solved L5 on the first attempt. L5 returns
to a single checked chain/guide pair (target 8->9->8) but splits the
movable rack with a fixed blocker at x=29, requiring a vertical detour
around it and staged assembly on different rows. Found a new
boundary-jamming asymmetry: during horizontal retraction a
boundary-blocked block stays fixed while the chain retracts through
it, but during perpendicular row movement an analogous blocked push
cancels the entire row move instead.

The source agent's own fresh-environment reproduction gate confirmed
reached_level=5 independently. The outer loop independently
re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=5,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: sk48 levels_reproduced 4 -> 5.
reproducible_total_levels 171 -> 172 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
