+    target guide order is 8->9->8, with three 9-blocks starting left
+    of the blocker and three 8-blocks starting right of it. The
+    blocker prevents forward extension across it on the rack row and
+    also prevents a long cross-divider carrier from moving
+    perpendicularly into that row -- the chain must detour vertically
+    around it, staging blocks on different rows before assembling the
+    target via endpoint passage and selective retraction. New
+    boundary-jamming subtlety confirmed: during horizontal retraction,
+    a covered block whose push is blocked by the PLAYFIELD BOUNDARY
+    stays fixed while the chain retracts through it, but during
+    perpendicular row movement, an analogous blocked push cancels the
+    ENTIRE row move instead (an asymmetry between the two movement
